.TH SESSLINT-STATS 1 "" "SessLint 0.5.0" "SessLint Manual"
.SH NAME
sesslint-stats \- [read\-only] Aggregate content\-free statistics over session files.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sesslint stats [\-\-agent {claude,codex,all}] [\-\-adapter {auto,canonical,claude\-code\-jsonl,codex\-rollout,openai\-agents}] [\-f | \-\-format {human,json}] [\-\-json] [\-o | \-\-output FILE] [\-q | \-\-quiet] [\-v | \-\-verbose] PATH...
.SH DESCRIPTION
[read\-only] Aggregate statistics over session files or directories: event counts by kind/actor, tool\-call volume per hashed tool name, compactions, checkpoints, size percentiles.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B PATH
Path(s) to session file(s) or directories (scanned recursively)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-agent {claude,codex,all}
Aggregate over a well\-known agent session root instead of paths Choices: claude, codex, all.
.TP
.B \-\-adapter {auto,canonical,claude\-code\-jsonl,codex\-rollout,openai\-agents}
Session format adapter for all inputs (default: auto) Choices: auto, canonical, claude\-code\-jsonl, codex\-rollout, openai\-agents. Default: auto.
.TP
.B \-f {human,json}, \-\-format {human,json}
Output format (default: human) Choices: human, json.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit sesslint.stats/v1 JSON (shortcut for \-\-format json)
.TP
.B \-o FILE, \-\-output FILE
Write the report to FILE instead of stdout (existing report files are overwritten atomically)
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Suppress non\-error stderr output
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Print debug diagnostics (settings provenance, elapsed) to stderr
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
a clean session exits 0
(also verification passed / dry-run plan generated)
.TP
.B 1
a session with findings exits 1
(also verification failed / repair refused)
.TP
.B 2
an internal tool error exits 2
(also usage error / invalid flags / I/O failure)
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled — interrupted via Ctrl+C or a cooperative cancellation request;
partial outputs are cleaned up.
.SH SEE ALSO
sesslint(1), sesslint\-bundle(1), sesslint\-check(1), sesslint\-completion(1).

.nf
Full documentation: the docs/ tree in the source repository
(docs/SPEC.md, docs/codes/, docs/recipes/, docs/adr/, docs/THREAT_MODEL.md),
or the project site.
.fi

